#==============================================================================================
#
#   html_select_element_1 - HTML::HTMLSelectElement: construction, options and selection
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of LibWeb/HTML/HTMLSelectElement.cpp (lines 1-489): the constructor (which moves
#       the mixin tables to HTMLSelectElement's, as C++'s vptrs move, and sets the legacy
#       platform object flags), initialize, visit_edges, the adjusted computed style, the
#       display size and size, the options collection with length, item, namedItem, add and
#       remove, the selected options, the list of options (cached), the reset algorithm,
#       selectedIndex, the children changed steps, type, the default role, and value.
#       html_select_element_2 has the picker, the shadow tree and the selectedness setting
#       algorithm; the inline functions of HTMLSelectElement.h are at its end.
#
#       Copyright (c) 2020, the SerenityOS developers.
#       Copyright (c) 2021-2022, Andreas Kling <andreas@ladybird.org>
#       Copyright (c) 2023, Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
